Selected Idea
-------------

A generic "Preserve Editorial Intent" rule can shift emphasis and introduce unsupported claims - a controlled prompt experiment
In a controlled comparison where the only change was adding a reusable Narrative instruction to "Preserve Editorial Intent from the Synthesis," candidate runs consistently shifted the top-level message away from company identity/audience and made orchestration the central positioning, while also introducing unsupported audience and validation claims. The change was the proximate variable and the experiment led to a rollback.

