### Unknowns

1. Whether the single change to Narrative.user.prompt.txt was the cause of the observed change in Narrative and Compose scores. (The source records the change and the score differences but does not establish causality.)

2. The specific mechanism(s) inside the model that produced the observed editorial drift (for example, which phrases or instructions in the added section drove the changes). (The source records the existence of the added section and behavioral outcomes but does not identify internal mechanisms.)

3. Whether backend changes to the model alias (gpt-5-mini) occurred during the experiment and affected outputs. (The report lists this as a limitation but does not report whether it happened.)

4. Whether results would replicate under more runs, different seeds/temperatures, or a different model alias. (The report notes three runs and lack of seed/temperature control but does not provide replication data.)

5. The complete verbatim content of every Narrative and Compose output beyond the summarized descriptions in the report. (The report states outputs are saved in artifacts but does not print them in full within this source text.)

6. Why orchestration became the central positioning in candidate outputs (motivation or internal reasoning is not established). (The report documents that orchestration became central but does not establish why.)

7. Whether any human editing occurred between generated outputs and the scored results. (The report does not state that human edits were applied to candidate outputs before scoring.)

8. Whether alternative prompt edits could have preserved editorial intent while remaining reusable. (The report tests one candidate change and does not evaluate alternatives.)


### Development sequence

1. Baseline prompts and production prompts were verified to match before the experiment. (Fact 7 and Fact 8)

2. Three baseline runs from a prior experiment snapshot were reused as the baseline condition. (Fact 10)

3. A candidate prompt change was made by adding a section titled "Preserve Editorial Intent from the Synthesis" to Narrative.user.prompt.txt. (Facts 11, 12, 13)

4. Three new candidate runs were executed with the candidate prompt; all other inputs and files were unchanged. (Facts 10 and 15)

5. All runs completed all workflow stages and exited 0; logs and outputs were saved. (Facts 17 and 18)

