7. The report documents that candidate Narrative and Compose outputs subordinated company identity/audience and made orchestration central, and that candidate outputs introduced unsupported validation/audience framing. (Facts 22, 25, 26, 27)

8. The analysis concluded the candidate prompt was not sufficient to protect the supplied editorial intent and noted Synthesis was outside the experiment's scope. (Fact 29)

